{{Quote|I used to bull's-eye womp rats in my T-16 back home.|Luke Skywalker|<ref name="Episode IV" />}}
'''T-16 skyhoppers''', also known as the '''T-16 airspeeders''', were [[skyhopper]]s, that were personal [[repulsorlift]] [[airspeeder]]s manufactured by [[Incom Corporation]], recognizable by its distinctive tri-wing design. It was a popular, high-performance airspeeder due to its stable and reliable transportation on almost any world, and thus provided many youths with their first flight training.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> The T-16's trihedral design greatly resembled that of the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle|''Lambda''-class T-4a shuttle]].<ref name="SW 15">[[Star Wars (2015) 15|''Star Wars'' (2015) 15]]</ref><ref name="Databank">{{Databank|imperial-shuttle|Imperial Shuttle}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:T-16_Skyhopper_TCG-TT.png|thumb|left|180px|A T-16 in landing configuration]]
[[Luke Skywalker]] owned a [[Luke's T-16 skyhopper|T-16 skyhopper]] on [[Tatooine]] prior to the [[Battle of Yavin]], as well as a small [[Luke Skywalker's T-16 skyhopper model|model]] that could be held in one's hands.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> He would use the airspeeder's [[pneumatic cannon]] to kill [[womp rat]]s. The controls were similar to Incom's [[T-65B X-wing starfighter]], which greatly benefited Skywalker during the Battle of Yavin.<ref name="Episode IV" />

{{Veh-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Here we actually have the broken T-16 skyhopper that Obi-Wan pulled out to repair for Luke.''"<br />"''Oh and there's little guys in the cockpit.''"<br />"''The actual T-16 skyhopper was researched and referenced to recreate this prop itself.|A member of the [[Lucasfilm Archives]] and [[Kristin Baver]] discussing the T-16 skyhopper toy prop used in ''Obi-Wan Kenobi''|<ref name="Props">{{ThisWeek|5dYCIFU5q6Y|Obi-Wan Kenobi Props, LEGO Star Wars Summer Vacation, and More!|sw_url=video/obi-wan-kenobi-props-lego-star-wars-summer-vacation-and-more}}</ref>}}
[[File:T-16SkyhopperToyPropKenobi.png|thumb|300px|The T-16 skyhopper toy prop used in ''Obi-Wan Kenobi''|left]]
The T-16 skyhopper first appeared in the [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], the first installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[original trilogy]].<ref name="Episode IV" /> It was first identified in the [[2015]] reference book ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" />

During production of the ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' television series, the prop making team made a broken T-16 skyhopper [[Luke Skywalker's T-16 skyhopper model|toy]] prop that was used in the series. The originial prop was researched and referenced to recreate the prop.<ref name="Props" />

===BT-16 reference===
{{Quote|I'll check out that T-16.|A stormtrooper|<ref name="Part III">{{Kenobi|Part III}}</ref>}}
The T-16 is mentioned by [[stormtrooper]]s in "[[Part III]]," the third episode of the series ''Obi-Wan Kenobi'', as a reference to a conversation in ''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'' between two stormtroopers who are discussing the [[BT-16]] while Obi-Wan Kenobi [[Rescue of Princess Leia|disables]] the [[tractor beam]]. References to that scene started by voice actor [[Sam Witwer]] who added similar lines in the [[sequel trilogy]], which mention the [[T-17]] and [[T-18]], and in ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'' and ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'', which mention the [[T-15]]. The mention depended on the era.<ref name="Sam Witwer">{{YouTube|video=Z8UdXvynS50|text=Sam Witwer - Matt Lanter - Star Wars Celebration 2022 - DAY 4 Panel|channel=UCX2BSSVDZbk5PrppNQREfTA|name=Super Steve|date=29-05-2022}}</ref> "[[Chapter 8: Redemption]]" of the series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'' mentions the T-16 in a similar fashion too.<ref name="Chapter 8">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 8: Redemption}}</ref>

===Non-canon appearances===
[[File:T-16 Skyhopper Pilot Luke Skywalker LEGO.png|thumb|The LEGO minifigure of the Skyhopper pilot|248x248px]]
[[LEGO]] released three [[LEGO Star Wars|LEGO ''Star Wars'']] sets of the T-16 skyhopper&mdash;one in [[2003]],<ref name="LEGO 4477">{{LEGOCite|num=4477|name=T-16 Skyhopper}}</ref> one in [[2015]]<ref name="LEGO 75081">{{LEGOCite|num=75081|name=T-16 Skyhopper}}</ref> and one in [[2020]].<ref name="LEGO 75265">{{LEGOCite|type=micro|num=75265|name=T-16 Skyhopper vs Bantha Microfighters}}</ref> The newer sets both feature a [[human]] pilot in a red [[jumpsuit]] and a grey safety [[harness]] with a grey [[helmet]] with two red insignias and a [[blaster pistol]].<ref name="LEGO 75081" /><ref name="LEGO 75265" /> While only identified as "Skyhopper Pilot", the 2015 ''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Visual Dictionary: Updated and Expanded]]'' implies that the "Mystery pilot" is Luke Skywalker.<ref name="CE 2015">''[[LEGO Star Wars: The Visual Dictionary: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref>

